    "show_share": true,
    "description": "OJ Riaga's journey from a local radio station in Kisumu to the global humanitarian organization Médecins Sans Frontières (MSF) is a testament to his passion for storytelling and his commitment to making a difference. His career began at Kenya's leading Dholuo FM radio station and the first audio-visual Radio in East and Central Africa, Ramogi FM, where he honed his skills as a journalist, covering a wide range of topics from local politics, sports politics and community events.",
